[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32918"] :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨2{t}^{2}\\,,\\,{e}^{t}\\,,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩$, find all of the points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are parallel." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,2{e}^{t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that $r({t}_{0})=c\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =c\\,{r}^{′}(t) \\\\ ⟨2{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t},\\,2{e}^{t}⟩ & =c\\,⟨4t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,2{e}^{t}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t},\\,2{e}^{t}⟩ & =⟨4ct,\\,c{e}^{t},\\,2c{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}=4ct \\\\ {e}^{t}=c{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}=2c{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we obtain that $c=1.$ Substituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2} & =1\\cdot 4t \\\\ {t}^{2} & =2t \\\\ {t}^{2}-2t & =0 \\\\ t(t-2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $r$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the points corresponding to $t=0$ and $2.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨2(0)^{2},\\,{e}^{0},\\,2{e}^{0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ r(2) & =⟨2(2)^{2},\\,{e}^{2},\\,2{e}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,{e}^{2},\\,2{e}^{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the points $(0,1,2)$ and $(8,{e}^{2},2{e}^{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-75203/selection/2ce734b435732dfc499a14ffed8c9dfd12051348f629c292b5655e9f60f51c31" :answer/id #uuid "5bb029d8-f44a-57f8-9b2a-b0c8da08d92a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩+u⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75203/selection/faeccca291b57ab909bf9b1086a1152a75c9c39e1b53e4ee4450b87caa9f86b1" :answer/id #uuid "8919beb2-2605-58ed-839d-0c399b920152" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩+u⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75203/selection/d82be93f054516ff9ac70a8a9228b987d00b3ca45e28dbce29819c086e66e91f" :answer/id #uuid "cd2dc8ff-4b91-51e3-af02-cc5df3908b97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,1,1⟩+u⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75203/selection/2c9acd929e58b3f68d7d6de34537f3853ba2607944f6a35c9a030c0f26def3e6" :answer/id #uuid "2c431266-4c36-5efa-9d12-b3c03dd77f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,1,1⟩+u⟨1,\\,-1,0⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75203/selection/8c9c3e85bab941971aba3e176d8633aa3f82f234601ab1c84c3ffd2a45eb294c" :answer/id #uuid "11a92c0f-7f2f-5703-bcca-37d080f7ea57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩+u⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75203/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "288cbfdd-3be2-5693-8506-6a82d50d6f5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75203/selection/faeccca291b57ab909bf9b1086a1152a75c9c39e1b53e4ee4450b87caa9f86b1" :answer-field/choices ["q-75203/selection/2ce734b435732dfc499a14ffed8c9dfd12051348f629c292b5655e9f60f51c31" "q-75203/selection/faeccca291b57ab909bf9b1086a1152a75c9c39e1b53e4ee4450b87caa9f86b1" "q-75203/selection/d82be93f054516ff9ac70a8a9228b987d00b3ca45e28dbce29819c086e66e91f" "q-75203/selection/2c9acd929e58b3f68d7d6de34537f3853ba2607944f6a35c9a030c0f26def3e6" "q-75203/selection/8c9c3e85bab941971aba3e176d8633aa3f82f234601ab1c84c3ffd2a45eb294c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75203" :question/id #uuid "f79a0634-b781-513c-bc7a-42650fc401f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75203" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t}⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=0$,  the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{0},\\,{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{-t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨1,\\,{e}^{0},\\,-{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point \n where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩+u⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75203/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75203"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126835/selection/b2bcd59bd54db66dde92d673d8daa7a800ec92c27f0b9dabb815f24a534ab3d0" :answer/id #uuid "4d3f6f05-e2b9-5329-9364-d0192d174f99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,-1⟩+u⟨3,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126835/selection/23fed8ff1732876450ae4b0ddaa771e26cccf8857bec75b5e14786fbb97878c2" :answer/id #uuid "d79405e0-cf4f-56f0-ba10-aaf9cddf88c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5,1⟩+u⟨3,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126835/selection/1f1687015fb975b2415544e6a6262566a0a52d1e2219264c10b07628568c26bc" :answer/id #uuid "19c9af6e-fd42-5fe8-a8a0-4ef5c76c9b79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5,1⟩+u⟨3,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126835/selection/0228dacd6c7f8b5bbb12587b243a31b873ef76f35b7f8bb20fc007d921c1f82f" :answer/id #uuid "cbd9cf26-36a3-573f-be14-4292f29ef821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,-1⟩+u⟨1,5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126835/selection/d20d2b44008be1fb2a6da02a4811079049150081cf72375518fb5fb7ff050b89" :answer/id #uuid "0d66860a-50b2-5812-a611-399d148a0e71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨5,1⟩+u⟨1,5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126835/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfba4061-161c-5e71-9c8e-3ddfb8354902" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126835/selection/1f1687015fb975b2415544e6a6262566a0a52d1e2219264c10b07628568c26bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-126835/selection/b2bcd59bd54db66dde92d673d8daa7a800ec92c27f0b9dabb815f24a534ab3d0" "q-126835/selection/23fed8ff1732876450ae4b0ddaa771e26cccf8857bec75b5e14786fbb97878c2" "q-126835/selection/1f1687015fb975b2415544e6a6262566a0a52d1e2219264c10b07628568c26bc" "q-126835/selection/0228dacd6c7f8b5bbb12587b243a31b873ef76f35b7f8bb20fc007d921c1f82f" "q-126835/selection/d20d2b44008be1fb2a6da02a4811079049150081cf72375518fb5fb7ff050b89"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126835" :question/id #uuid "28b07468-67e6-5160-b480-58f04dacf3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-126835" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨3t+5,1-{t}^{3}⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=0,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨3(0)+5,1-{0}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨3,-3(0)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨5,1⟩+u⟨3,0⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-126902"] :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨2{t}^{2}-t,5-3{t}^{2}⟩,$ find the point at which the tangent to the curve is parallel to the vector $⟨-1,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5-3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t-1,-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $⟨-1\\,,\\,2⟩$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})=c⟨-1,2⟩.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =c⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\ ⟨4t-1,-6t⟩ & =c⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\ ⟨4t-1,-6t⟩ & =⟨-c,2c⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4t-1=-c \\\\ -6t=2c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain that $c=-4t+1.$ Substituting $c=-4t+1$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6t & =2(-4t+1) \\\\ -6t & =-8t+2 \\\\ 2t & =2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $⟨-1,2⟩$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=1.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨2(1)^{2}-1,5-3(1)^{2}⟩=⟨1,2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨-1,2⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $(1,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-164840/selection/2360981b27d03f67e0b3ff56682d40bc54f15f3e409a4f41e41f75acb780e398" :answer/id #uuid "e2033a63-1ab3-5f1e-99af-a83fcad0e314" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(7,9)$ and $(14,16)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164840/selection/3daf7c7813fd10d96af0e7397ad761fd8013a7868d9b6c8ad4b2e20ce2d33dca" :answer/id #uuid "27768cb2-e09c-5f1e-863e-f00fbca3eafe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164840/selection/1905ba85551ade1a8c1dbddfaf3642be86682bfcda82bed5923dc149b188d0c4" :answer/id #uuid "8e0ba96f-fca2-5b85-a4a8-c7ca577b4743" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,4)$ and $(-1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164840/selection/7d721447c74511cc7ce1dd365eb9260ed7acbcf4fe9ece91f3ee8c2e43a7d309" :answer/id #uuid "2de6936d-188d-5b1b-92bb-57ef40e0405f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164840/selection/ef73e093dc4d40e56262dbdf8089db1df51b0c9578b85e73d7052576c2d277c2" :answer/id #uuid "cbe7a385-9e89-5968-927b-cfb29a8fb0d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(14,16)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164840/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "43088988-e045-502f-b9da-394309ab53c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164840/selection/7d721447c74511cc7ce1dd365eb9260ed7acbcf4fe9ece91f3ee8c2e43a7d309" :answer-field/choices ["q-164840/selection/2360981b27d03f67e0b3ff56682d40bc54f15f3e409a4f41e41f75acb780e398" "q-164840/selection/3daf7c7813fd10d96af0e7397ad761fd8013a7868d9b6c8ad4b2e20ce2d33dca" "q-164840/selection/1905ba85551ade1a8c1dbddfaf3642be86682bfcda82bed5923dc149b188d0c4" "q-164840/selection/7d721447c74511cc7ce1dd365eb9260ed7acbcf4fe9ece91f3ee8c2e43a7d309" "q-164840/selection/ef73e093dc4d40e56262dbdf8089db1df51b0c9578b85e73d7052576c2d277c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164840" :question/id #uuid "0d4944e3-e48d-5ad3-888c-09e6883cda6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164840" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=({t}^{2}-2)\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ $t\\in (0,\\infty )$, find all of the points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are perpendicular." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ [({t}^{2}-2)\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j]\\cdot (2t\\,i+2t\\,j) & =0 \\\\ ({t}^{2}-2)\\cdot 2t+{t}^{2}\\cdot 2t & =0 \\\\ 2t(2{t}^{2}-2) & =0 \\\\ 4t({t}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ 4t(t-1)(t+1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\in (0,\\infty )$, the only solution is $t=1.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =((1)^{2}-2)\\,i+(1)^{2}\\,j=-\\,i+j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(-1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-164840/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "297a4812-a87a-592a-818a-8c8d3d3f7868"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164840"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
